I think this might be a good spot to raise the question: How much do
stats really matter in Nethack, after a certain point?  (Assume we're
discussing vanilla here.)

I mean, STR/CON are helpful to increase carrying capacity, but everyone
eventually goes for the bag of holding anyway, which is far more
valuable than STR/CON.  Even before then, the Gauntlets of Power are an
effective solution to "I can't carry nothin'".

INT/WIS are for the casters, but the Hat of Smart at +5 takes care of
most of those problems; what it won't handle, the robe will, and so much
for spell failure percentages.  If you're not a caster, who cares?  (I'm
looking at you here, Mister Int 6 Barbarian.)

DEX is nice for hitting things, but a luckstone and maxed-out luck takes
care of that quite nicely with the 65% bonus to hit; XL 7 takes care of 
the remaining 35% and there you go.

And that leaves CHA, of course, the "nearly meaningless stat".

While it's all well and good to worry that it may be too easy to go from
16 to 17 by simply pushing rocks, the real question might be: does it
even matter that someone can go from 16 to 17?

With apologies to someone who asked the same question of me in
#sporkhack recently: How much would the game really change if all stats
were capped, hard, at 15?  I suspect the answer to that is "not that
much, really" -- meaning that perhaps a better course would be to make
there be a more significant difference between 15 and 18 in each stat 
prior to making it harder to get from 15 to 18.

